From: OpenDesk <opendesk>
Date: 2026-04-02
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Fix SIGABRT crash on ButtonMove — HaveMouseCapture() root cause fix

ROOT CAUSE (diagnosed via MNP-TOUCH hilog logs in patch 0005):
  - HaveMouseCapture() always returned false (hardcoded)
  - ButtonDown called SetMouseCapture(true) but we ignored it
  - ButtonMoveWithModifiers checks HaveMouseCapture():
    * true  → safe branch: selection adjustment only
    * false → dangerous branch: hover/cursor detection via PositionFromLocation
      → AutoSurface creation → SurfaceImplOHOS::Init(wMain.GetID())
      → OH_Drawing/Skia internal state conflict → abort()
  - Down succeeded because it never checks HaveMouseCapture()
  - Move crashed 2ms after DoButtonMove ENTER (confirmed by hilog logs)

FIX:
  - Add mouseCaptured bool member to ScintillaOHOSEditor
  - SetMouseCapture(bool on) now sets mouseCaptured = on
  - HaveMouseCapture() now returns mouseCaptured
  - This routes ButtonMove into the safe "captured" code path

DIAGNOSTICS retained from patch 0005:
  - OH_LOG_Print hilog diagnostics remain for verification
  - AbortGuard sigaction+siglongjmp remains as safety net

Files: ohos/ScintillaOHOS.cxx

